{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nF28A and F45 are approved with the operator correction. GitHub Actions is active and supplies Verified. GitHub Issues is disabled. The operator confirmed that a future integration is planned. No dedicated implementation record was found in the tracker during this survey, so this story does not add an unsupported ticket citation. Current runbooks also describe inactive Verified enforcement, obsolete vote carry, and prior submit behavior. The committed desired state is `infra/gerrit/project.config`.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Update `infra/runbooks/github-mirror-lock.md` with the current GitHub Actions and GitHub Issues posture.\n- State that future GitHub Issues integration is planned without presenting it as available or citing an unidentified record.\n- Update `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md` and `infra/runbooks/two-vote-gate-rollback.md` from `infra/gerrit/project.config`.\n- Document that `LLM-Review` must reach MAX and carries across `NO_CODE_CHANGE`, `MERGE_FIRST_PARENT_UPDATE`, and `TRIVIAL_REBASE`.\n- Document that `Verified` must reach MAX and carries across `NO_CODE_CHANGE` and `TRIVIAL_REBASE`, but not `MERGE_FIRST_PARENT_UPDATE`.\n- Document that both label functions use `NoBlock` while submit requirements enforce both votes. The `LLM-Review` requirement also rejects unresolved comments.\n- Document `rebase if necessary` as the submit action.\n- Preserve Gerrit-only merging and rollback procedures.\n- Make no service setting changes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `infra/runbooks/github-mirror-lock.md` states that GitHub Actions remains enabled and supplies Verified.\n- [x] `infra/runbooks/github-mirror-lock.md` states that GitHub Issues is disabled and that future integration is planned but unavailable.\n- [x] Runbook descriptions of both labels and their submit requirements match `infra/gerrit/project.config`.\n- [x] Runbook descriptions of each label copy condition match `infra/gerrit/project.config`.\n- [x] Submit guidance reflects the `rebase if necessary` action in `infra/gerrit/project.config`.\n- [x] Gerrit-only merging and rollback procedures remain intact.\n- [x] Only `infra/runbooks/github-mirror-lock.md`, `docs/gerrit-aws-setup.md`, and `infra/runbooks/two-vote-gate-rollback.md` change.\n- [x] Focused documentation, ADR, link, and whitespace checks pass. The full local test suite is skipped.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Compare the edited guidance with the `LLM-Review`, `Verified`, submit-requirement, and submit sections of `infra/gerrit/project.config`.\n- Run the focused documentation, ADR, link, and whitespace checks used by the repository."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787606209379033001,"uuid":"1c38ff39-d170-4acc-96e3-ce4b0a242cb6"}